"""Round 27: the declared changes to the Papyrus sources the historical verifiers accept. GENERATED by
build/fix27_history_gen.py from this template -- edit the reasons there, never the digests here.

Round 27 moves the form switch into the DLL (G8: the switch task leaves, marks, enters and bursts; Papyrus only swaps the
ability, plays the sounds and keeps its sync rules through ESSBNative.KeepSync), shows where to look when the DLL was
refused (G12), and plays the end / open effects on a target the DLL's own damage just killed (G13). No property or
variable changed (the state schema stays). The round-27 seal (build/fix26_history.py) now runs on the pre-fix27 snapshot
(.codex/pre-fix27-snapshot/src, taken before any round-27 edit), and this module proves that today's scripts differ from
that snapshot ONLY by the changes declared below, each bound to the code by digest (comment-stripped body, sha256[:16],
build/fix21_history.digest):

  CHANGED     (script, function) -> (why, before, after)
  REMOVED     (script, function) -> (why, before)
  ADDED       (script, function) -> (why, after)
  PROPERTIES  script -> (why, code lines added outside functions, code lines removed)
  FILES       whole scripts removed or added -> (why, sha256 of the file, 'removed' | 'added')

Anything else fails the build. legacy_source() hands the older seals and verifiers the snapshot only after that proof;
the chain is fix21 -> ... -> fix26 (25 -> 26, "now" = pre-fix27) -> this one (26 -> 27, "now" = src/).
The round-27 behaviour itself is checked by build/fix27_verify.py and the native runtime test.
"""
